# 1️⃣7️⃣ PCA IS NOT FEATURE SELECTION

Very important distinction.

### Feature selection

Keeps original features:

```text
Age
Salary
Experience
```

Maybe selects:

```text
Age
Salary
```

---

### PCA

Creates completely new features:

```text
PC1
PC2
PC3
```

Each component can be a combination of many original features.

Therefore:

> PCA is **feature transformation**, not simply feature selection.

---

# 1️⃣8️⃣ PROJECTION

PCA ultimately projects data onto the selected principal components.

Imagine:

```text
        •
      •
    •
  •
──────────────────
        PC1
```

Instead of representing each point with:

```text
x + y
```

we represent it primarily along:

```text
PC1
```

So a 2D dataset can become:

```text
2D → 1D
```

while preserving as much variance as possible.

